# The Codex review of 2026-11-19, finding 3: a password field a page turned to text before its submit (a "show
# password" button) must not put the password into the form history. jihad-login.html's form with the password shown:
# with no password field at the submit there is no login to save (no question asked), and about:data's form history
# then holds the note and the username but never the password.
id: site-data-shown-password
section: Privacy and site data
item: A login form submitted with its password shown as text (a page's "show password"): no login question, and the form history (about:data) keeps the note and the username but not the password
shells: enyo mochi mojo
prefs: jihad.compat.trace=true signon.rememberSignons=true browser.formfill.enable=true
page: http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-login.html
kit: cavekit-site-data.md R3
fixture: site-data-clean
wait rect user 30
probe submit '(function(u,p){document.getElementById("user").value=u;var q=document.getElementById("pass");q.value=p;q.type="text";document.getElementById("note").value="shown note";return "filled "+u+", the password shown";})("jihad-shown","shown-pass-9")'
tap go
wait text sent "sent jihad-shown" 15
expect dialog none 4
launch about:data?pane=forms
wait text forms "shown note" 10
expect text-has forms "jihad-shown"
expect text-lacks forms "shown-pass-9"
tap 'sel:.forms-remove-all'
wait text forms-remove-all-row "entries?" 4
tap 'sel:.forms-remove-all'
wait text forms "Nothing typed" 6
